WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.796
"Oh, I'm not in the mood".

00:00:09.339 --> 00:00:11.591
Who here has ever
told a partner that before?

00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:13.218
(Laughter and murmuring)

00:00:16.012 --> 00:00:17.597
We've all done this.

00:00:17.639 --> 00:00:20.809
And if you haven't said it,
then you've probably heard it.

00:00:21.726 --> 00:00:23.144
Intuitively, we understand

00:00:23.186 --> 00:00:25.897
that our minds matter
when it comes to sex,

00:00:25.897 --> 00:00:29.776
but we’re quick to focus
on bodies, touch and sensation

00:00:29.776 --> 00:00:32.028
as the most crucial elements.

00:00:32.028 --> 00:00:36.032
We're less likely to consider
the role of our imaginations.

00:00:36.032 --> 00:00:39.494
In many parts of our life,
we are really great at imagining.

00:00:39.494 --> 00:00:44.124
Things like vacations
or dream homes or career moves.

00:00:44.165 --> 00:00:48.378
These exercises in imagination
help us define what it is we want.

00:00:49.254 --> 00:00:51.298
They allow us to flirt
with what's possible

00:00:51.339 --> 00:00:53.925
before having to make any decisions.

00:00:53.967 --> 00:00:56.886
And they're also innately pleasurable,

00:00:56.928 --> 00:00:59.681
even if those fantasies
never actually materialize.

00:01:00.599 --> 00:01:02.809
Imagination is such a powerful tool.

00:01:02.851 --> 00:01:07.147
So when it comes to sex, why isn't it
one of the first ones that we reach for?

00:01:08.773 --> 00:01:11.526
When I first started doing research
on arousal and desire,

00:01:11.526 --> 00:01:15.614
I learned that for women,
cognition is as important to arousal

00:01:15.614 --> 00:01:17.657
as the presence of sexual stimuli.

00:01:18.533 --> 00:01:23.913
In other words, using their memories,
fantasies and some focus,

00:01:24.706 --> 00:01:27.042
women can turn themselves on
with their thoughts.

00:01:28.752 --> 00:01:30.962
This particular study focused on women,

00:01:31.004 --> 00:01:35.008
and much of my own work is also focused
on people who are female identifying.

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:38.637
But this much is clear
regardless of gender identity:

00:01:38.678 --> 00:01:40.972
the brain is the biggest sex organ,

00:01:41.014 --> 00:01:44.476
and everyone can benefit
from expanding their sexual imagination.

00:01:45.685 --> 00:01:46.936
I first started thinking

00:01:46.978 --> 00:01:49.272
about this connection
between sex and imagination

00:01:49.272 --> 00:01:50.565
while I was in college.

00:01:50.565 --> 00:01:52.734
Back then, among my friends,

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:55.862
the definition of sex
was extremely narrow.

00:01:55.862 --> 00:02:00.450
It essentially meant penetrative sex
between a guy and a girl.

00:02:01.576 --> 00:02:04.454
And masturbation
wasn't a topic of conversation.

00:02:05.497 --> 00:02:09.542
Frankly, I think that solo sex
was seen as a last resort,

00:02:09.584 --> 00:02:11.378
a desperate or lonely act

00:02:11.419 --> 00:02:14.381
instead of a fundamentally
empowering exploration.

00:02:15.715 --> 00:02:17.801
One morning, a friend of mine
was telling me

00:02:17.842 --> 00:02:20.345
about her latest unsatisfying hookup,

00:02:20.387 --> 00:02:23.473
and I asked her what
she had been thinking about during sex.

00:02:24.683 --> 00:02:26.685
"Hmm," she said.

00:02:28.353 --> 00:02:29.562
“I don’t know.”

00:02:30.772 --> 00:02:33.316
Something about that really struck me.

00:02:33.316 --> 00:02:36.820
Her entire memory of the experience
was what had happened physically.

00:02:37.696 --> 00:02:41.658
So many of us think that good sex
is something that should happen to us,

00:02:41.658 --> 00:02:44.202
that it’s in someone else’s hands,
quite literally,

00:02:44.786 --> 00:02:48.957
We expect a partner, current or future,
to be the magical unlock.

00:02:49.457 --> 00:02:52.252
Maybe because we feel
especially safe with them

00:02:52.293 --> 00:02:53.962
or attracted to them

00:02:54.003 --> 00:02:56.715
or because they have
more experience than we do.

00:02:56.756 --> 00:03:01.052
But in doing so, we forget
our own agency in the matter.

00:03:01.094 --> 00:03:06.099
We write ourselves and our imaginations
out of the pleasure equation.

00:03:07.726 --> 00:03:09.394
I had this hunch that my friend,

00:03:09.436 --> 00:03:13.565
that many of us, were experiencing
a crisis of inspiration.

00:03:14.774 --> 00:03:16.151
In the years after college,

00:03:16.151 --> 00:03:19.571
my fascination with the role
of imagination and sexuality only grew.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:25.535
Eventually, I left the career I'd built
to start a company called Dipsea,

00:03:25.535 --> 00:03:30.790
which creates stories, audio stories,
designed to turn women on.

00:03:32.125 --> 00:03:34.252
I decided to focus on audio

00:03:34.294 --> 00:03:39.048
because it's so immersive
and so evocative and so personal.

00:03:39.924 --> 00:03:41.426
Here's what I mean.

00:03:41.468 --> 00:03:45.346
Feel free to close your eyes
and consider where these sounds take you.

00:03:46.431 --> 00:03:47.682
(Birds chirping)

00:03:47.724 --> 00:03:49.392
(Water flowing)

00:04:01.154 --> 00:04:02.989
OK. Open your eyes.

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:05.575
Were those not the sounds
you were imagining I'd play?

00:04:05.575 --> 00:04:07.368
(Laughter)

00:04:07.368 --> 00:04:09.662
Here's what comes to my mind.

00:04:09.662 --> 00:04:11.206
I'm in the mountains.

00:04:11.247 --> 00:04:13.541
I can feel the sunshine on my face.

00:04:13.583 --> 00:04:16.878
I can feel the cool chill
coming up off the Alpine water.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.672
I can see the tiny flecks
of sparkle in the granite.

00:04:20.715 --> 00:04:25.553
I bet that every person in this room
is imagining something a little different,

00:04:25.595 --> 00:04:28.890
but filled with all sorts of distinct
details about the surroundings,

00:04:28.932 --> 00:04:30.391
about the circumstances.

00:04:31.184 --> 00:04:33.061
Audio is incredible that way.

00:04:34.103 --> 00:04:38.024
Erotic audio stories
have characters and plot,

00:04:38.024 --> 00:04:42.570
but like the sounds you just heard
create a blueprint for your mind

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:44.197
to then fill in the blanks.

00:04:44.864 --> 00:04:47.826
They allow you to develop
your own vision of what's appealing

00:04:47.826 --> 00:04:49.244
in a way that can get lost

00:04:49.244 --> 00:04:53.498
when you see something specific
or explicit onscreen.

00:04:54.916 --> 00:04:56.793
You may not be ready or interested

00:04:56.835 --> 00:04:59.087
in dipping a toe
into erotic audio stories.

00:04:59.128 --> 00:05:00.380
And that's OK.

00:05:00.421 --> 00:05:02.465
So today I'm going to walk you through

00:05:02.507 --> 00:05:04.926
how you might get started
creating your own stories

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:07.136
and activating
your own sexual imagination.

00:05:07.762 --> 00:05:11.099
I won't take this too far.
You don't have to follow along right now.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:13.101
But consider this a guide

00:05:13.142 --> 00:05:15.311
for the next time
you get a little me time.

00:05:16.688 --> 00:05:17.939
(Laughter)

00:05:18.773 --> 00:05:20.859
First, you'll want to settle
into your mind

00:05:20.859 --> 00:05:23.069
the same way that you
might start a meditation.

00:05:24.612 --> 00:05:26.948
Then imagine that your mind
is like a projector.

00:05:26.948 --> 00:05:30.702
Everything you can see and experience
is what's right in front of you.

00:05:30.702 --> 00:05:33.496
Everything to your left,
right, behind you,

00:05:33.496 --> 00:05:34.747
that's out of frame.

00:05:35.498 --> 00:05:38.751
This is important because
while there are thoughts that turn us on,

00:05:38.793 --> 00:05:43.298
there are also thoughts that are
incredibly effective at turning us off:

00:05:43.339 --> 00:05:46.885
stress, shame, insecurities,

00:05:46.926 --> 00:05:50.346
and also the things
that inexplicably ick us out.

00:05:51.139 --> 00:05:54.267
So when a thought appears
that isn't working,

00:05:54.309 --> 00:05:56.269
and it inevitably will,

00:05:56.311 --> 00:05:59.230
you'll be able to sweep it out of frame.

00:06:00.648 --> 00:06:02.817
You can start with your senses.

00:06:02.817 --> 00:06:06.696
Imagine colors, textures, sounds, images,

00:06:06.696 --> 00:06:08.656
anything that gives you sensory pleasure.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:12.327
Sometimes I like to imagine
cherry blossoms

00:06:12.327 --> 00:06:14.787
softly floating down from trees.

00:06:14.787 --> 00:06:19.834
Or I use a fiery pinkish orange
or a relaxing blue as a backdrop

00:06:19.876 --> 00:06:21.711
for the experience that I'm imagining.

00:06:22.712 --> 00:06:24.339
Next, try places.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.883
And keep in mind that setting
will be more important

00:06:26.925 --> 00:06:28.551
to some of us than to others.

00:06:28.593 --> 00:06:29.969
Reach back into your memory

00:06:30.011 --> 00:06:32.764
to that secluded beach
you visited many years ago.

00:06:32.805 --> 00:06:37.018
Or create a setting from scratch
with as much privacy and comfort,

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:40.521
or as many adventurous stakes as you like.

00:06:41.606 --> 00:06:44.692
Next think about a person
and layer on a narrative.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.946
Maybe it's a character
from one of your favorite books.

00:06:48.863 --> 00:06:50.406
Maybe it's your girlfriend.

00:06:51.491 --> 00:06:53.993
Hey, maybe it's a guy in a kilt.

00:06:54.661 --> 00:06:57.747
Whoever it is, how do they approach you?

00:06:57.789 --> 00:06:59.040
What's motivating them?

00:06:59.082 --> 00:07:01.292
What energy are they coming to you with?

00:07:01.334 --> 00:07:03.586
What about you? What do you say?

00:07:03.628 --> 00:07:05.004
And what do you do together?

00:07:05.546 --> 00:07:07.924
And when you find something
that you really like,

00:07:07.966 --> 00:07:09.258
play it out for a while.

00:07:10.093 --> 00:07:12.053
You’ll have just designed your own story.

00:07:12.637 --> 00:07:14.305
The more you flex this muscle,

00:07:14.347 --> 00:07:16.683
the more you'll understand
what turns you on

00:07:16.724 --> 00:07:19.769
and be able to communicate
those things to a partner.

00:07:19.811 --> 00:07:23.064
You can share the entire fantasy
with them if you're comfortable.

00:07:23.064 --> 00:07:26.901
That kind of disclosure
can be very intimate and affirming.

00:07:28.027 --> 00:07:29.278
Or ...

00:07:29.946 --> 00:07:31.197
don't.

00:07:32.115 --> 00:07:35.243
It is not a betrayal
to use your imagination

00:07:35.243 --> 00:07:37.286
to bring you more pleasure.

00:07:37.286 --> 00:07:39.622
Fantasy is a safe space,

00:07:39.664 --> 00:07:43.334
and it's time we bust the myth
that what you fantasize about

00:07:43.376 --> 00:07:45.670
and what you want to happen in reality

00:07:45.712 --> 00:07:46.963
are always the same thing.

00:07:48.131 --> 00:07:53.052
So allow me to offer us
a bigger definition of what sex is.

00:07:54.053 --> 00:07:56.723
Sex isn't just a physical act.

00:07:56.764 --> 00:07:58.891
It's a mental experience.

00:07:58.933 --> 00:08:01.561
And it isn't wholly
dependent on a partner.

00:08:01.602 --> 00:08:03.354
It starts with you.

00:08:03.354 --> 00:08:07.191
You're the one in control
of creating the most pleasure for you.

00:08:07.191 --> 00:08:09.235
You're the protagonist.

00:08:09.235 --> 00:08:12.613
As much as you love someone
or feel attracted to them,

00:08:12.613 --> 00:08:15.199
they are playing a supporting role.

00:08:15.199 --> 00:08:16.451
And you for them.

00:08:17.702 --> 00:08:22.957
Sex is an avenue to accessing feelings
of aliveness, empowerment,

00:08:22.999 --> 00:08:24.709
joy and confidence

00:08:24.751 --> 00:08:26.419
innate to all of us.

00:08:26.961 --> 00:08:31.591
That aliveness,
that is the impact of sexual wellness.

00:08:31.632 --> 00:08:34.093
And you will feel it
walking down the street,

00:08:34.135 --> 00:08:37.221
entering any conversation,
navigating any relationship.

00:08:38.723 --> 00:08:39.974
Put that way,

00:08:40.016 --> 00:08:43.144
none of us can afford
not to prioritize sex.

00:08:43.186 --> 00:08:45.938
It isn't a nice-to-have
or an if-I-get-to-it,

00:08:45.938 --> 00:08:49.150
dead last on our list
right after picking up the dry cleaning.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:51.486
So the next time you notice

00:08:51.486 --> 00:08:53.905
that you haven't been
in the mood for a while,

00:08:53.905 --> 00:08:55.823
carve some time out for yourself

00:08:55.823 --> 00:08:59.452
and let your imagination
tell you a sexy story.

00:09:00.411 --> 00:09:01.704
Thank you.

00:09:01.704 --> 00:09:06.501
(Applause)

